00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.660
Spoiler warning: Obviously, I'm discussing
The Last Jedi in full detail so take care

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.040
if you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.190
The final scenes of the movie are set on Crait,
where the Resistance finds itself holed up

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.550
in an old Rebel base.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:52.181
Their shield-door has been destroyed by the
First Order's siege cannon, the First Order

00:00:52.181 --> 00:00:55.440
is amassed outside, and there's no apparent
means of escape.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.160
The Resistance is in a desperate situation
as they discover nobody is responding to their

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.810
distress signal, a sign that as Leia says
"the galaxy has lost all hope."

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.420
Then out of nowhere Luke appears and has a
touching reunion with his sister.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.460
No one in the Resistance knows it yet, but
at this point Luke has force-projected himself

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.340
out of his own body which is still on Ahch'To.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.640
Luke's force projection is able to physically
interact with events on Crait, for example

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.689
fighting Kylo Ren in a lightsaber duel, while
his physical body is still on the island.

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:28.649
This is something new we've not seen before
in the Star Wars movies, however, something

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:34.189
similar has been seen in the Star Wars Expanded
Universe, aka Star Wars Legends, where such

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:37.850
projections are known as Force Phantoms or
Sith Phantasms.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:42.710
Basically, they're apparitions created by
Darksiders in a Sith ritual that harnesses

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.030
the Force Energy from another being.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.050
The apparitions can then be projected across
the universe and used to interfere in the

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:53.789
physical realm, and when the phantom is destroyed
so is the lifeform which supplied its Force

00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:54.789
Energy.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:59.700
Also, in the Star Wars Dark Empire comic books,
Luke has created a projection of himself in

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.039
order to help Leia escape.

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:06.389
The Star Wars Legends universe is no longer
canon, however, but it's interesting to see

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:10.090
elements from it included with a twist in
The Last Jedi.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.560
Given that Force Projection is new to The
Last Jedi, I think we're likely to see more

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.840
of it going forward in new Star Wars movies,
perhaps even with characters like Rey and

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.959
Kylo Ren as their powers grow stronger.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:25.920
OK, so getting back to that confrontation
on Crait between Luke and Kylo Ren, we need

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.150
to analyse Luke's words in more detail.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.760
Luke says to Kylo that "the Rebellion is reborn
today, the war is just beginning, and I will

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.140
not be the last Jedi".

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:39.599
At this moment, the camera cuts to Rey who's
discovered that the Resistance are stuck in

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:42.330
the old Rebel base behind a pile of rocks.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.400
Rey then uses the Force to move the rocks
away and, given Luke's words, we've got a

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.850
clear indication that Rey will be the face
of the new Jedi.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.280
The moment is also a nice call-back to earlier
in the movie when Luke was teaching Rey about

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.829
the Force and explained that it's not about
lifting rocks, which itself was a reference

00:02:58.829 --> 00:03:02.340
to The Empire Strikes Back when Luke trained
with Yoda.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.230
When the scene cuts back to Luke and Kylo
facing off, Kylo vows to destroy everyone

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:11.780
and, in a moment that's very reminiscent of
Obi Wan Kenobi and Darth Vader in A New Hope,

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.030
Luke turns off his lightsaber and says to
Kylo, "Strike me down in anger and I'll always

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.920
be with you, just like your father."

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.390
And as Luke disappears from Crait, we cut
back to the island where Luke is levitating.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.560
The effort of the force projection causes
Luke to collapse back on to the rock.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.019
We then get a very emotional scene as Luke
looks out across the water and a cloud passes

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:33.159
over the sun.

00:03:33.159 --> 00:03:37.430
Then Luke vanishes, leaving behind just his
robes, becoming one with the Force, in the

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:41.900
same way that Obi Wan vanished when Darth
Vader struck him down in A New Hope and also

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.269
how Yoda passed away in Return of the Jedi.

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:49.569
Luke's sacrifice to save the Resistance, allowing
them to escape the First Order, also mirrors

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:53.489
Obi Wan's sacrifice which allowed Han, Leia,
and Luke to escape Vader.

00:03:53.489 --> 00:03:58.159
This is a heart-breaking scene for many fans,
but there's some important visual symbolism

00:03:58.159 --> 00:03:59.159
here too.

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:03.420
Luke's sacrifice brought some balance back
as the First Order was about to snuff out

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.769
the Resistance before his intervention, and
the cloud partially obscuring the sun suggests

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:10.940
the light and the darkness in some sort of
balance.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.000
At one point in this sequence, what looked
like a faint rainbow appeared in the sky.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.530
Not only can it be a sign of hope, change,
and a bridge between worlds, but also in the

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:23.490
Buddhist tradition, a rainbow body is a state
of enlightenment when a person achieves the

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:28.050
highest state of meditation and complete knowledge,
and is often said to happen around the time

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.780
of death, with the body dissolving into light.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:35.199
The Jedi way in Star Wars borrows from various
Eastern religions and philosophies, one of

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:39.320
which is Buddhism, so I think the rainbow
symbolism goes perfectly with the idea of

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.870
Luke having reached a higher state with his
ability to force project himself and then

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.530
when he becomes one with the Force at the
end.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.770
Later in the scene, we also see the two suns
on the horizon, which is another nostalgic

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.800
call-back to when Luke walked out on Tatooine
in A New Hope and looked out over the sunset.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.010
I'm pretty sure Luke will return in Episode
9 though, most likely as a Force Ghost, with

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:04.400
an ongoing ability to participate and influence
events.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.319
Yoda already came back as a Force Ghost in
The Last Jedi and set the Force Tree on fire

00:05:09.319 --> 00:05:13.750
and I think we could see Luke have new scenes
with Rey and Kylo in the next movie; after

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.020
all, his parting words to Kylo were "see you
around kid."

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.670
Luke's death was also sensed by Rey and Leia
and, although it's a poignant moment, Rey

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:25.509
does say that she didn't sense sadness or
pain, but peace and purpose.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:29.660
However, that still leaves Rey wondering at
the end how they will rebuild the Resistance.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:34.730
Leia answers that they "have everything [they]
need" and the camera pans down to Rey holding

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.759
Luke's old lightsaber which was split in two
earlier in the movie when she struggled with

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:40.949
Kylo Ren for control of it.

00:05:40.949 --> 00:05:45.080
Inside one of the lightsaber halves you can
see an exposed Kyber crystal.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:49.139
Although Kyber crystals have appeared in other
Star Wars media, in the movies they were first

00:05:49.139 --> 00:05:53.120
introduced in Rogue One where the Empire was
amassing them for the construction of the

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.630
Death Star.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:59.570
Kyber crystals are a crucial element in constructing
lightsabers as they help to concentrate energy

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.639
into the weapon's blade.

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:06.199
In the animated Clone Wars TV series, new
Jedi younglings have been involved in gathering

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:09.009
kyber crystals to build their own lightsabers.

00:06:09.009 --> 00:06:13.070
And so, I think Leia's words along with the
visual of the Kyber crystal indicate we could

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:17.170
see Rey start a new Jedi Academy to fight
back against the First Order.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:21.699
Or, perhaps, the kyber crystals will be key
to some new Resistance technology that we've

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:25.860
not yet seen in the Star Wars universe, in
a similar way to how they were crucial to

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.509
the Empire in operating the Death Star superweapon.

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:34.500
By the way, just before Rey boarded the Millennium
Falcon, she and Kylo were still able to sense

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.500
each other.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:40.120
Earlier, Snoke claimed he was responsible
for bridging Kylo and Rey's minds, but with

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.479
Snoke dead by the end of the movie, it seems
that either Snoke was manipulating and lying

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:48.849
to them and/or that Kylo and Rey's abilities
have increased and so they can now connect

00:06:48.849 --> 00:06:51.250
with each other, independent of anyone else.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:55.810
However, the way Rey closes the Millenium
Falcon's door during their final connection

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:59.450
might mean she's closing off future communication
with Kylo.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:04.580
Although we see Kylo continue to embrace the
dark side throughout The Last Jedi, he is

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:08.620
still conflicted, for example, hesitating
to kill his mother Leia.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:13.280
And I wonder if, given that Luke told Leia
"no one's ever really gone", we may see Kylo

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.419
redeem himself in some way by the end of Episode
9, as Darth Vader/Anakin Skywalker did by

00:07:17.419 --> 00:07:21.479
the end of Return of the Jedi, though if this
did happen I would expect there to be a spin

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:24.229
on it to make it at least a bit different.

00:07:24.229 --> 00:07:29.120
Of course, Luke's line that "no one's ever
really gone" also refers to Han Solo, and

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:33.060
Luke hands Leia the dice from the Millennium
Falcon just after saying this.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:38.380
But Luke's words also foreshadow his own sacrifice
at the end of the movie and his likely return

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.860
in Episode 9.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.690
Before we leave Crait, we need to talk about
Finn and Rose.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:48.030
In contrast to his attempt to leave the Resistance
early on in the film, Finn ends up willing

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.669
to sacrifice himself for the cause when he
speeds towards the First Order's mega cannon,

00:07:52.669 --> 00:07:57.289
and although I never believed Episode 8 would
be the end for Finn, director Rian Johnson

00:07:57.289 --> 00:07:59.069
did manage to rack up the tension.

00:07:59.069 --> 00:08:04.800
But Rose drops in literally crashing his speeder
off course and then unexpectedly kisses him.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.040
It's interesting that Finn and Rose's last
major scene together calls back to their first

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.819
scene, which also featured Rose scuppering
Finn's plans when she stopped him leaving

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:13.819
in an escape pod.

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:18.590
But a lot's changed since then, and Finn has
stepped up, proving worthy of Rose's high

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:23.470
opinion of him as a hero and Rose herself
has proven worthy of the title 'hero' as well.

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.310
And Rose's line to Finn that they would win
by saving what they love, not by fighting

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:31.939
what they hate, was a positive moment amid
a bleak situation for the Resistance, and

00:08:31.939 --> 00:08:35.860
echoes what Luke was taught by Yoda and Obi
Wan about not giving in to hate.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.260
I wasn't necessarily expecting the movie to
pair up Rose and Finn, but given they did,

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:44.440
it's a nice touch that she ends the film healing
up, similar to how Finn finished his story

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.790
in The Force Awakens.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:50.541
Those were the final scenes with the main
cast, but just before the credits roll, we

00:08:50.541 --> 00:08:55.700
get an important short scene set back on Canto
Bight, where we see the stable hands re-enacting

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.660
the events on Crait with their own handmade
toys.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:02.860
The scene shows that news and stories of how
the legendary Jedi Master stood up to Kylo

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.920
Ren and the First Order have spread through
the galaxy, reigniting the spark that will

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.411
light the fire to burn the First Order down,
as Poe Dameron says at the end of the movie,

00:09:11.411 --> 00:09:14.190
in an echo of Vice Admiral Holdo's words.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:18.780
One of the boys then goes outside and as he's
force sensitive he calls a broom to him, then

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.850
looks up and sees a streak of light flash
across the sky.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:26.480
We can then see that he's wearing the old
Rebellion ring that Rose Tico gave him earlier

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.480
in the movie.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:30.990
It's a moment filled with hope and confirms
Luke's claim to Kylo Ren that "the Rebellion

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:32.220
is reborn".

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:36.279
By the way, according to the Visual Dictionary,
the boy's name appears to be Temiri Blagg,

00:09:36.279 --> 00:09:40.200
and I wonder whether he will actually be a
specific new force user who will appear in

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.000
either Episode 9 or the new trilogy that Rian
Johnson is developing after JJ Abrams' film.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:50.320
If he is going to appear again, then we may
well revisit Canto Bight in a future movie.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:55.170
Also, I think it's intriguing that this boy,
like Rey, has been sold and abandoned by his

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.769
parents, which means we're getting a theme
in Star Wars that a Force User doesn't always

00:09:58.769 --> 00:10:02.430
need to inherit their Force abilities from
a special or privileged family.

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:07.300
This scene also hints that we may get a time
jump between the end of The Last Jedi and

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.300
Episode 9.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:12.220
This would allow time for stories to spread
about Luke Skywalker and the Resistance and

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.200
how they foiled the First Order.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:19.070
A time gap could also be a possible way to
deal with Leia's story in Episode 9 and the

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:22.720
fact that Carrie Fisher is sadly no longer
with us.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.200
And if you're interested in my thoughts and
theories on how I think we'll see Leia's arc

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.300
completed in the sequel, then tap in the top
right or check the video description for my

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.060
Carrie Fisher video.

